use std
into hair.amni

Imports: os, binary, gfx, math, gfx.linalg, gfx.gltf, gfx.motion and gfx.scene3d. This file is a module with no main.

Struct `HairU` holds view_proj, view and proj (each `gfx::mat4`), then size, cam, to_sun, sun_rgb, hair, sky, params and look (each `float4`), then light_vp (`gfx::mat4`), light (`float4`), shadow_vp (`gfx::mat4`), mel (`float4`), pl (`float4[8]`) and shape (`float4`), in that order, matching the GLSL uniform block `Hair` in shaders/strand_common.glsl.

`mel_of(c float3, bn f32) float2` turns a hair color into eumelanin and pheomelanin concentrations (Chiang et al. 2016): with `d = 5.969 - 0.215 bn + 2.532 bn^2 - 10.73 bn^3 + 5.574 bn^4 + 0.245 bn^5`, the absorption wanted per channel is `s = (ln(max(c, 0.001)) / d)^2`; fit `s ≈ e * (0.419, 0.697, 1.37) + p * (0.187, 0.4, 1.05)` by least squares (solve the 2 x 2 normal equations); when e or p comes out negative, set it to 0 and refit the other alone (`dot(s, v) / dot(v, v)`, at least 0); return (e, p).

Module state: `var on = false`, `var hair_top f32 = 0.0` (the largest y of any guide point), `var hair_col = float3 { 0.58, 0.38, 0.14 }`, `var hair_gain f32 = 1.0`, `var hair_sun = float3 { -1.0, 0.0, 0.0 }` (a key light color for the strands that stands in for the sun's color when its x is not negative), `var guides = 0`, `var parts = 0`, `var cells = 0`, `var sdf_done = false`, `var sim_reset = true`, `var probe_ask = false`, `var probe_v f32[>..]` (eight probe results), `var hm_prev = gfx::mat4_identity`, `var part_node int[>..]` (global glTF node of each collision part), `var part_ib gfx::mat4[>..]` (its inverse bind matrix), `var simv float4[>..]` (the simulation table, 120 entries, laid out as the `Sim` buffer of shaders/strand_body.glsl), `var tgt`, `var st`, `var gd`, `var simb`, `var sdfb`, `var trib`, `var statb` (`gfx::Buffer`), `sim_p`, `sdf_p` (`gfx::ComputePipeline`), `var w = 0`, `var h = 0`, `var spc = 96`, `var points = 0`, `var segments = 0`, `var center = float3 { 0.0, 0.0, 0.0 }`, `var bones = 0` (spring-bone count), `var bone_node int[>..]` (glTF node index of each bone, local to the asset), `var mats gfx::mat4[>..]` (one matrix per bone), and `var` handles `pts`, `rest`, `skin`, `matsb`, `segs`, `front`, `acc`, `lfront`, `lacc` (`gfx::Buffer`), `hairt` (`gfx::Texture`), `smp` (`gfx::Sampler`), `comp` (`gfx::Pipeline`), `clear_p`, `raster_p`, `resolve_p`, `skin_p` (`gfx::ComputePipeline`, what `gfx::compute_pipeline` returns, assigned directly), each starting from `default<T>()`.

`hair_size(nw int, nh int)` sets w and h and (re)creates the screen-sized resources: with `rw = gfx::BUFFER_COMPUTE_WRITE | gfx::BUFFER_COMPUTE_READ`, `front = gfx::buffer(rw, nw * nh * 4, [])`, `acc = gfx::buffer(rw, nw * nh * 64, [])` and `hairt = gfx::texture(gfx::TextureDesc { format: gfx::RGBA16F, usage: gfx::SAMPLED | gfx::COMPUTE_WRITE, width: nw as i32, height: nh as i32 })` (gfx::buffer always takes three arguments; an empty slice zero-fills).

`hair_open(path const byte[:], nw int, nh int, strands int) bool` reads the guides file with the unqualified `read_file(path, data)` into a `byte[>..]` (false: return false) and returns `hair_load(data, nw, nh, strands)`.

`hair_load(data const byte[:], nw int, nh int, strands int) bool` sets the hair up from guide data. Layout: 4 magic bytes, "HMG2" or "HMG3" (byte 3 is 50 or 51), then little-endian i32 guides, points, segments at bytes 4, 8, 12 (read with `binary::gather(data, at, 4) as int`), then points × 48 bytes, then segments × 16 bytes; an HMG3 file then has an i32 bone count `bones` at `e = 16 + points * 48 + segments * 16`, `bones` i32 node indices after it (append each to `bone_node`), then points × 16 bytes of skin data starting at `k = e + 4 + bones * 4`. Set `points`, `segments`, `spc = strands` (but when any segment's third i32, at byte `16 + points * 48 + s * 16 + 8`, is above 0, `spc` is the largest such value instead: those segments carry their own child count); `pts = gfx::buffer(gfx::BUFFER_COMPUTE_READ | gfx::BUFFER_COMPUTE_WRITE, points * 48, data[16..16 + points * 48])`, `tgt` the same way (the animated targets), `st = gfx::buffer(<same usage>, points * 32, [])` (simulated positions and previous positions), `segs = gfx::buffer(gfx::BUFFER_COMPUTE_READ, segments * 16, <the segment bytes>)`. When `bones > 0`: `rest = gfx::buffer(gfx::BUFFER_COMPUTE_READ, points * 48, data[16..16 + points * 48])`, `skin = gfx::buffer(gfx::BUFFER_COMPUTE_READ, points * 16, data[k..k + points * 16])`, resize `mats` to `bones` entries of `gfx::mat4_identity`, `matsb = gfx::buffer(gfx::BUFFER_COMPUTE_READ, bones * 64, [])` and `skin_p = gfx::compute_pipeline(embed_shader("shaders/strand_skin.comp"))`. `hair_top` is the largest second f32 (y) of every point and `center` is the mean of the first three f32 of every point (point k at byte 16 + k*48, each `binary::f32_from_bits(binary::gather(data, at, 4) as! u32)`). Light buffers: `lfront = gfx::buffer(rw, 512 * 512 * 4, [])`, `lacc = gfx::buffer(rw, 512 * 512 * 64, [])`. `smp = gfx::sampler(gfx::NEAREST, gfx::CLAMP)`; `comp = gfx::pipeline(embed_shader("shaders/strand_comp.vert"), embed_shader("shaders/strand_comp.frag"), gfx::PipelineDesc { blend: gfx::BLEND_PREMULTIPLIED })`; `clear_p`, `raster_p`, `resolve_p` with `gfx::compute_pipeline(embed_shader(...))` of "shaders/strand_clear.comp", "shaders/strand_raster.comp", "shaders/strand_resolve.comp". Guides: walk the segments in order (segment s has its point index at byte `16 + points * 48 + s * 16` and its guide number 4 bytes later); a new guide starts at the first segment and whenever the guide number differs from the previous segment's, with first point that segment's point and count 2, and every further segment of the same guide adds 1 to the count. Keep them as four i32 per guide in an `i32[>..]` list (first point, point count, skinned flag, 0), where the skinned flag is 1 when the file has bones and some point k of the guide has skin weights (the f32 at bytes `k * 16 + 8` and `k * 16 + 12` of the skin data, decoded with `binary::f32_from_bits`) adding up to more than 0.001, else 0. Set `guides` to the count, `gd = gfx::buffer(gfx::BUFFER_COMPUTE_READ, guides * 16, bytes_of(<that list>))`, `statb = gfx::buffer(gfx::BUFFER_COMPUTE_READ | gfx::BUFFER_COMPUTE_WRITE, guides * 16, [])`, `simb = gfx::buffer(gfx::BUFFER_COMPUTE_READ, 120 * 16, [])`, resize `simv` to 120 zero `float4`s and `probe_v` to 8 zeros, `sim_p = gfx::compute_pipeline(embed_shader("shaders/strand_sim.comp"))` and `sdf_p = gfx::compute_pipeline(embed_shader("shaders/strand_sdf.comp"))`. Until `hair_body` runs, `sdfb` and `trib` are `gfx::buffer(gfx::BUFFER_COMPUTE_READ | gfx::BUFFER_COMPUTE_WRITE, 16, [])` placeholders. Call `hair_size(nw, nh)`, set `on = true`, return true.

`skin_joint(sk int, node int) int` returns the k below `gltf::skins[sk].joints.count` with `gltf::ints[gltf::skins[sk].joints.first + k] == node`, or -1.

`tri_owner(v0 int, v1 int, v2 int) int` returns the skin joint with the largest weight summed over the three global vertices' four influences: keep parallel lists `js int[>..]` and `ws f32[>..]`; for each vertex v and c in 0..3, `j = gltf::verts[v * gltf::VERTEX_FLOATS + 18 + c] as int` and `w = gltf::verts[v * gltf::VERTEX_FLOATS + 22 + c]`, add w to the entry of j (pushing a new entry when j is not yet listed); return the j with the largest summed weight (-1 when the lists are empty).

`tri_box_hit(tl const float4[:], k int, lo float3, hi float3) bool` is true when the box of triangle k (the xyz of `tl[3k]`, `tl[3k + 1]`, `tl[3k + 2]`) padded by 0.035 on every side overlaps the box from lo to hi.

`hair_find_cards(asset int) bool` looks for the asset's own hair cards (the builder's groom: a mesh named "hair" made of strips, vertex pairs left/right along each card with uv v rising from root to tip) and remembers them in the module vars `card_node` and `card_mesh` (both `var`, starting at -1). Find the first node n of the asset with `mesh >= 0` and mesh name "hair" (false when none); `pr = gltf::prims[gltf::meshes[mesh].prims.first]`; it is card strips when `pr.vcount` is even and at least 4, `pr.icount >= 6`, the first six indices (`gltf::indices[pr.ifirst + i]`) are 0, 1, 2, 1, 3, 2, and for every pair k below `pr.vcount / 2` the uv v (float `gltf::AT_UV0 + 1`) of vertex `pr.vfirst + 2k` and of `pr.vfirst + 2k + 1` differ by less than 0.0001. When it is, set `card_node = n`, `card_mesh = mesh` and return true; else false.

`hair_card_data(asset int, data byte[>..]&) bool` makes guide data from the cards found by `hair_find_cards` into data (cleared first; false when `card_node < 0`), with no GPU work; `hair_cards(asset int, nw int, nh int, strands int) bool` calls it and returns false when it does, else `hair_load(data, nw, nh, strands)`. `pr = gltf::prims[gltf::meshes[card_mesh].prims.first]`, `n = card_node`. Vertex floats are at `v * gltf::VERTEX_FLOATS`: position `gltf::AT_POS`, uv `gltf::AT_UV0`, color `gltf::AT_COL`, joints `gltf::AT_JOINT` (floats), weights `gltf::AT_WEIGHT`. The head's joint is `hj = skin_joint(sk, gltf::find_node(asset, "head"))` with `sk = gltf::nodes[n].skin` (hj = -1 when sk < 0 or there is no head). Bones: every joint j (other than hj) that some hair vertex has with weight above 0.01, in order of first appearance, at most 64, kept as joint indices `bj` and as node indices local to the asset `bn` (`gltf::ints[gltf::skins[sk].joints.first + j] - gltf::assets[asset].nodes.first`). Cards: walk the pairs in order; a new card starts at pair 0 and whenever a pair's v is smaller than the previous pair's v. For each card with at least 2 pairs (pairs a .. e - 1), for each of its pairs k with left vertex `l = pr.vfirst + 2k` and right `r = l + 1`: `c = (P(l) + P(r)) / 2`, `sd = (P(r) - P(l)) / 2`, the tangent `tg` is `c(k1) - c(k0)` with `k0 = max(k - 1, a)` and `k1 = min(k + 1, e - 1)` (never evaluate c outside a .. e - 1), `nm = linalg::unit3(cross3(tg, sd))`, `t = (v(k) - v(a)) / max(v(e - 1) - v(a), 0.000001)`, `occ = (red(l) + red(r)) / 2`; append the twelve floats c.x, c.y, c.z, occ, sd.x, sd.y, sd.z, t, nm.x, nm.y, nm.z, 0 to an `f32[>..]` `pf`; and for the skin, add up the weights of l and r on each bone of `bj` (halved), take the two largest (bone list index and weight; index 0 and weight 0 when there are fewer) and append them to an `i32[>..]` `ki` (two entries) and an `f32[>..]` `kw` (two entries). For every pair of the card but the last append to an `i32[>..]` `sg` the four values (point index of the pair, card number, 0, 0), where point indices count all points appended so far and the card number counts the cards kept. Assemble the data as a `byte[>..]`: the 4 bytes of "HMG3", then the i32s cards, points, segments (append `bytes_of` of an `i32[>..]` of the three), then `bytes_of(pf)`, then `bytes_of(sg)`, then the i32 bone count and the `bn` list, then per point the four 4-byte words `ki[2p]`, `ki[2p + 1]` (as i32) and `kw[2p]`, `kw[2p + 1]` (as f32), built as a `f32[>..]` of 4 per point where the two index words are `binary::f32_from_bits(ki[..] as u32)`. Print "hair cards: " cards " guides, " points " points, " bones " bones" and return true.

`hair_body(asset int)` builds the collision body: one signed distance grid per body part, each rigid with one skin joint, in the skin's bind space (the space the strands are stored in). Return when `!on`. Let `n0 = gltf::assets[asset].nodes.first` and `nc = gltf::assets[asset].nodes.count`; `sn = gltf::find_node(asset, "skin")`; return when `sn < 0 || gltf::nodes[sn].mesh < 0 || gltf::nodes[sn].skin < 0`; `sk = gltf::nodes[sn].skin`.
Parts: `var pj int[>..]`; for each name in the list "head", "neck_01", "spine_03", "spine_02", "clavicle_l", "clavicle_r", "upperarm_l", "upperarm_r": `nd = gltf::find_node(asset, name)`; when `nd >= 0` and `k = skin_joint(sk, nd)` is `>= 0`, push nd to `part_node`, `gltf::matrices[gltf::skins[sk].inverse_binds.first + k]` to `part_ib` and k to `pj`. `parts = part_node.len`.
Boxes: `var lo float3[>..]` and `var hi float3[>..]`, one per part, starting at `float3 { 1e9, 1e9, 1e9 }` and `float3 { -1e9, -1e9, -1e9 }`.
Triangles: `var all float4[>..]`. For each n from n0 to n0 + nc - 1 with `gltf::nodes[n].mesh >= 0` and `gltf::nodes[n].skin == sk`, let `mn = gltf::text_of(gltf::meshes[gltf::nodes[n].mesh].name)`; skip unless mn is "skin", "face", "scalp" or "tank". For each primitive index q from `gltf::meshes[m].prims.first` for `.prims.count` (with `pr = gltf::prims[q]`) and each t below `pr.icount / 3`: `v0`, `v1`, `v2` are `pr.vfirst + gltf::indices[pr.ifirst + 3 * t + c] as int` for c = 0, 1, 2; positions `pa`, `pb`, `pc` are the floats 0..2 at `v * gltf::VERTEX_FLOATS`. `j = tri_owner(v0, v1, v2)`; `ow` = the index i in pj with `pj[i] == j`, or -1. Push `float4 { pa.x, pa.y, pa.z, ow as f32 }`, `float4 { pb.x, pb.y, pb.z, 0.0 }`, `float4 { pc.x, pc.y, pc.z, 0.0 }` to `all`; when `ow >= 0` grow `lo[ow]` and `hi[ow]` (component min and max) by pa, pb and pc.
Grids: `var tl float4[>..]`; `cells = 0`; for each part p: `o = 20 + 12 * p`. When `lo[p].x < hi[p].x`: `a = lo[p] - float3 { 0.035, 0.035, 0.035 }`, `b = hi[p] + float3 { 0.035, 0.035, 0.035 }`, `sz = b - a`, `cell = max(0.007, max(sz.x, max(sz.y, sz.z)) / 63.0)`, `gx = (sz.x / cell) as int + 2` and likewise gy, gz; `t0 = tl.len / 3`; for each triangle k below `all.len / 3` with `tri_box_hit(all[..], k, a, b)` push its three entries to `tl`. Otherwise `a = float3 { 0.0, 0.0, 0.0 }`, `cell = 0.007`, gx = gy = gz = 2 and `t0 = tl.len / 3`. Then `simv[o] = float4 { a.x, a.y, a.z, cell }`, `simv[o + 1] = float4 { gx as f32, gy as f32, gz as f32, cells as f32 }`, `simv[o + 2] = float4 { t0 as f32, (tl.len / 3 - t0) as f32, 0.0, 0.0 }` and `cells += gx * gy * gz`.
Hair color: for the first mesh m of the asset (from `gltf::assets[asset].meshes.first` for `.meshes.count`; look at the meshes, not the nodes, because the view has already taken the hair cards off their node) whose name is "hair", when `gltf::prims[gltf::meshes[m].prims.first].material >= 0`, set `hair_col` to that material's base rgb. Finally `simv[8].w = parts as f32`, `simv[14] = float4 { cells as f32, 0.0005, 0.004, 1.0 }`, `trib = gfx::buffer(gfx::BUFFER_COMPUTE_READ, max(tl.len, 1) * 16, bytes_of(tl))`, `sdfb = gfx::buffer(gfx::BUFFER_COMPUTE_READ | gfx::BUFFER_COMPUTE_WRITE, max(cells, 1) * 8, [])`, `sdf_done = false`, and print "hair body: " parts " parts, " cells " cells, " tl.len / 3 " triangles".

`hair_probe(k int) f32` asks for a probe of the simulation and answers from the last one: it sets `probe_ask = true` and returns `probe_v[k]` when k is 0..7, else 0. The probe values are 0 points inside the body (not counting roots), 1 roots inside the body, 2 mean tip distance from the styled target in millimeters, 3 the largest tip distance, 4 the mean sideways (x) tip offset in millimeters, 5 the number of probes taken, 6 guides.

`hair_bone(i int) int` returns `bone_node[i]`, and `hair_pose(i int, m gfx::mat4)` sets `mats[i] = m` (a bone's motion, in the head's rest space) when `i` is in range.

`hair_style(o float4)` sets hair_col to `float3 { o.x, o.y, o.z }` when o.x >= 0, and hair_gain to `max(o.w, 0.0)`.

`hair_draw(model gfx::mat4, dt f32)` simulates the strands for a frame of dt seconds and draws them (stored in the head's rest space) moved by `model`, onto `s3d::hdr_target()`; call it between `s3d::render_begin()` and `s3d::render_end(...)`. Return when `!on`. Let `im = linalg::inverse(model)`. Fill `var u = default<HairU>()`: view_proj `gfx::mul(s3d::view_proj_nj, model)`, view `gfx::mul(s3d::view_mat, model)`, proj `s3d::proj_mat`; size (w, h, spc, segments, all `as f32`); cam: `e = linalg::point(im, s3d::view.eye)` as (e.x, e.y, e.z, 0.7); to_sun: `t = gfx::mul(im, float4 { s3d::sun.to_sun.x, s3d::sun.to_sun.y, s3d::sun.to_sun.z, 0.0 })`, `ld = linalg::unit3(float3 { t.x, t.y, t.z })`, stored as (ld, 0); sun_rgb: `sc = if hair_sun.x >= 0.0 { hair_sun } else { s3d::sun.rgb }`, stored as (sc.x, sc.y, sc.z, 0); hair (hair_col, 0.42); mel: `m = mel_of(hair_col, 0.3)` as (m.x, m.y, 0.3, `min(s3d::lights.len, 4) as f32`); for each i below that count, `pl[2 i] = (linalg::point(im, s3d::lights[i].pos), s3d::lights[i].range)` and `pl[2 i + 1] = (s3d::lights[i].rgb / max(hair_gain, 1.0), 0)` (the gain brightens the hair under the sun and sky but leaves the rim and fill lights as they were); sky (0.12, 0.13, 0.15, 40.0); params (0.004, 1.7, 0.004, 0.00007); look (hair_gain, 1.0, 0.0, 0.7); shape (hair_top, center.z, 0.0035, 0) (the part line); light_vp `gfx::mul(gfx::perspective(0.24, 1.0, 2.0, 4.0), gfx::look_at(center + ld * 3.0, center, float3 { 0.0, 1.0, 0.0 }))`; light (512, 512, 0.35, 256 / tan(0.12)) all `as f32`; shadow_vp `gfx::mul(s3d::cascade_vp[0], model)`. Each compute pass: `gfx::begin_compute(...)`, `gfx::bind(pipeline)`, set `u.look.z` to the mode, `gfx::uniforms(gfx::COMPUTE, 0, u)`, ..., `gfx::end_compute()`; every storage buffer is bound with `gfx::bind_storage_buffer(gfx::COMPUTE, slot, buffer)` (there is no `gfx::bind_buffer`). The distance-grid pass and the simulation pass have no uniform block: do not call `gfx::uniforms` in them. A nested `fn raster(rw0 gfx::Buffer, rw1 gfx::Buffer, ro0 gfx::Buffer, ro1 gfx::Buffer, mode int)` runs one raster pass: read-write [rw0, rw1], raster_p, `gfx::bind_texture(gfx::COMPUTE, 0, s3d::nd_target(), smp)`, `gfx::bind_texture(gfx::COMPUTE, 1, s3d::shadow_map, smp)`, storage buffers 0..3 = pts, segs, ro0, ro1, dispatch ((segments + 63) / 64, spc, 1). Order: first, when `bones > 0`, skin the strand targets: `gfx::update_buffer(matsb, 0, bytes_of(mats)[..bones * 64])`, then a compute pass with read-write buffers [tgt], skin_p, `u.size.w = points as f32` before its `gfx::uniforms`, storage buffers 0..2 = rest, skin, matsb, dispatch ((points + 63) / 64, 1, 1), and set `u.size.w = segments as f32` back after it. Then simulate: let `reset = sim_reset || dt <= 0.0 || length3(model.c3.xyz - hm_prev.c3.xyz) > 0.5`; when reset set `hm_prev = model`. Fast turns: `var carry = gfx::mat4_identity`; with `de = gfx::mul(model, linalg::inverse(hm_prev))`, `ang = acos(clamp((de.c0.x + de.c1.y + de.c2.z - 1) / 2, -1, 1))` (computed in `real`, then `as f32`) and `ax = float3 { de.c1.z - de.c2.y, de.c2.x - de.c0.z, de.c0.y - de.c1.x }`; when `!reset && ang > 0.2`: `k = 1 - 0.2 / ang`, `qe = linalg::qaxis(if length3(ax) > 0.001 { linalg::unit3(ax) } else { float3 { 0.0, 1.0, 0.0 } }, ang * k)`, `c = hm_prev.c3.xyz`, `mv = (model.c3.xyz - c) * k`, and `carry = gfx::mul(gfx::translate(c + mv), gfx::mul(linalg::qmatrix(qe), gfx::translate(float3 { -c.x, -c.y, -c.z })))`; then set `hm_prev = gfx::mul(carry, hm_prev)`. This carries the strands rigidly through whatever part of a frame's turn is more than 0.2 radians, so the solver only ever sees a small turn. Set `simv` entries 116..119 to the columns of `carry`. Fill `simv`: entries 0..3 the columns c0..c3 of `model`, 4..7 those of `im`, `simv[8] = float4 { dt, if reset { 1.0 } else { 0.0 }, 0.0, parts as f32 }`, `simv[9] = float4 { 0.0, -9.81, 0.0, guides as f32 }`, 10..13 the columns of `hm_prev`, `simv[15] = float4 { 0.1, 0.35, 0.08, 0.5 }` (shape stiffness at the tip and at the root, then the same for guides on spring bones), `simv[16] = float4 { 0.25, 0.9, 0.0, 0.02 }` (bend stiffness, length-correction damping, unused, velocity damping); `simv[17] = float4 { 0.007, hair_top - 0.07, hair_top - 0.02, 0.0 }` (crown lift and the heights it ramps over); for each part p with `o = 20 + 12 p` and `mp = gfx::mul(motion::world[part_node[p]], part_ib[p])`, entries `o + 3 .. o + 6` the columns of `linalg::inverse(mp)` and `o + 7 .. o + 10` those of `mp`. `gfx::update_buffer(simb, 0, bytes_of(simv))`. When `!sdf_done && cells > 0`, build the distance grids once: a compute pass with read-write buffers [sdfb], sdf_p, storage buffers 0..1 = trib, simb, dispatch ((cells + 63) / 64, 1, 1), and set `sdf_done = true`. Then a compute pass with read-write buffers [st, pts, statb], sim_p, storage buffers 0..3 = tgt, gd, simb, sdfb, dispatch ((guides + 63) / 64, 1, 1). Set `sim_reset = false` and `hm_prev = model`. When `probe_ask`: read the per-guide results with `gfx::read_buffer(statb, 0, raw[..])` into a `byte[>..]` `raw` of guides * 16 bytes; with four little-endian u32 per guide (`binary::gather(raw, at, 4)`), set `probe_v[0]` to the sum of the first, `probe_v[1]` the sum of the second, `probe_v[2]` the mean of the third divided by 1000, `probe_v[3]` the largest third divided by 1000, `probe_v[4]` the mean of (the fourth minus 1000000000) divided by 1000 (all as f32), add 1 to `probe_v[5]`, set `probe_v[6] = guides as f32` and `probe_ask = false`. Then clear [front, acc] mode 0 dispatching ((w*h + 63) / 64, 1, 1); clear [lfront, lacc] mode 2 dispatching ((512*512 + 63) / 64, 1, 1); raster(lfront, lacc, front, acc, 2); raster(lfront, lacc, front, acc, 3); raster(front, acc, lfront, lacc, 0); raster(front, acc, lfront, lacc, 1); resolve with buffers [] and textures [hairt] (two-list `gfx::begin_compute`), resolve_p, mode 1, storage buffer 0 = acc, dispatch ((w + 7) / 8, (h + 7) / 8, 1); then `if gfx::begin_pass(gfx::PassDesc { color: [s3d::hdr_target(), gfx::Texture{0}, gfx::Texture{0}, gfx::Texture{0}], clear_color: false, .. })` { `gfx::bind(comp)`, `gfx::bind_texture(gfx::FRAGMENT, 0, hairt, smp)`, `gfx::draw(3)`, `gfx::end_pass()` }.
